  "description": "Move two indices toward each other or in same direction to shrink the search space without extra memory.",
  "coreIdea": "Two indices = O(n) instead of O(n²). Use when array is sorted OR when you need pairs/triplets.",
  "whenToUse": [
    "Finding pairs with target sum in sorted array",
    "Removing duplicates in-place",
    "Palindrome checking",
